{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790348155,"nonce":"iA0VtlNWS9AsIVoK1DKYGUlpdJA=","title":"Split bytecode images: malformed input panics or silently drops functions","message":"On a Split (format 3) image whose CRC is valid but whose contents are malformed:\n- stripped() and shell() panic through expect (crates/compiler/src/bytecode.rs:299-302, :313-315).\n- into_module, and so deserialize_module on a Split image, silently drops a function whose body fails to decode (:286-291, :415-421).\n- by_id and by_name are only length-checked (:523): an out-of-range position panics at :281/:287, and unsorted arrays make lookups silently wrong.\n\nA reader of untrusted or corrupted input should return an error for each of these. Validate positions and sortedness once at load, and make a body that fails to decode an error, not a missing function.","files":null}]}